== CoCo Lifecycle Evidence Log: MCP CONNECTOR (INGENUITY BONUS) ==
Phase: INGENUITY BONUS — MCP External Tool Integration
Session: coco_mcp_session.log
Date: 2026-09-29
Connection: WZ37797 (Snowflake)
CLI Tool: Snowflake CoCo / Cortex CLI

================================================================================
1. OBJECTIVE
================================================================================
Demonstrate MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration by building a lightweight
MCP server that exposes supply chain OTD breach detection as tools invokable
from CoCo CLI. This turns read-only analytics into actionable alerting.

This satisfies the hackathon requirement: "Connecting to additional sources via
MCP: Wire in external systems and tools through MCP so the agent can read from
and act across those tools" and "MCP connectors to external tools: Extend the
solution by connecting CoCo to additional data sources and tools through MCP."

================================================================================
2. MCP SERVER IMPLEMENTATION
================================================================================
File Created:
  mcp/supply_chain_mcp_server.py (189 lines)

Technology:
  - MCP Python SDK v2.2.0 (MCPServer with stdio transport)
  - snowflake-connector-python 4.7.5
  - Connection via ~/.snowflake/connections.toml

Tools Registered:
  1. check_otd_breach(supplier_id: str)
     - Queries V_SLA_VS_ACTUAL_OTD for a specific supplier
     - Returns alert payload with SLA target, actual OTD, gap, status
     - Includes escalation recommendation based on breach severity
     - Alert levels: CRITICAL (breach), WARNING (within 3pts), OK (meeting)

  2. sla_compliance_report()
     - Returns full SLA compliance summary across all 20 suppliers
     - Includes breach/warning/meeting counts
     - Top 5 breaching suppliers with gap analysis
     - Top 3 performing suppliers

================================================================================
3. MCP CONFIGURATION
================================================================================
Project Config:
  mcp/mcp_config.json

CoCo CLI Global Config:
  ~/.snowflake/cortex/mcp.json

Configuration:
  {
    "mcpServers": {
      "supply-chain-alerts": {
        "command": "<venv>/python3",
        "args": ["<project>/mcp/supply_chain_mcp_server.py"],
        "env": { "SNOWFLAKE_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_NAME": "WZ37797" }
      }
    }
  }

Transport: stdio (standard MCP transport for CoCo CLI)

