================================================================================
6. COCO CLI INVOCATION
================================================================================
CoCo CLI Integration:
  When CoCo CLI is launched with MCP enabled (via ~/.snowflake/cortex/mcp.json),
  the supply-chain-alerts server starts automatically as a stdio subprocess.

  CoCo recognizes the tools and can invoke them via natural language:
    User: "Check if Siemens Industrial is breaching their delivery SLA"
    CoCo: [calls check_otd_breach("SUP-009")] -> Returns CRITICAL alert

  This enables conversational supply chain monitoring directly in the terminal:
    User: "Which suppliers need corrective action plans?"
    CoCo: [calls sla_compliance_report()] -> Returns breach list with recommendations

Launch Command:
  cortex --mcp  (or just 'cortex' if mcp.json is in ~/.snowflake/cortex/)

